    """
    Compute mean, sum, max, min and population standard deviation for keys 'x','y','z'
    from a list of dictionaries `d`.

    Attempts to use polars if installed (Polars is a modern DataFrame library; many
    releases and improvements continued in 2024+). If polars is not available, falls back
    to a pure-Python computation.

    Returns a dict like:
      { 'x': {'mean':..., 'sum':..., 'max':..., 'min':..., 'std':...},
        'y': {...},
        'z': {...} }

    Any metric for which there are no numeric values will be None.
    The standard deviation returned is the population standard deviation (division by n).
    """
    cols = ("x", "y", "z")

    # Helper to compute stats from an iterable of numbers (assumes floats)
